:false,"italic":false,"size":8.49,"text":"the Assessing Officer may impose a penalty of Rs. 100000 on such person.\""},{"bbox":[44.93,78.67,51.8,86.5],"bold":false,"font":"LiberationSerif","furniture":false,"italic":false,"size":7.07,"text":"11"},{"bbox":[76.5,17.17,221.38,33.52],"bold":true,"font":"NotoSans-Bold","furniture":true,"italic":false,"size":12.0,"text":"Income Tax Department"},{"bbox":[76.5,33.13,249.06,45.39],"bold":false,"font":"NotoSans-Regular","furniture":true,"italic":false,"size":9.0,"text":"Ministry of Finance, Government of India"}],"text":"Penalty for failure to furnish report under section 172.\n447. \n[***]\n11. Omtt. by Act No. 4 of 2026, w.e.f. 1-4-2026. Prior to its omission, section 447 read as under :\n\"447. Penalty for failure to furnish report under section 172.—If any person fails to furnish a report from an accountant as required by section 172,\nthe Assessing Officer may impose a penalty of Rs. 100000 on such person.\"\n11\nIncome Tax Department\nMinistry of Finance, Government of India\n"}